  m_Name: CentrifugalPumpData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Centrifugal Pump
  engineDescription: "A centrifugal pump is a hydraulic machine that converts the
    mechanical energy of a rotating impeller into pressure energy to transport liquids.
    Its main components are the impeller, casing, shaft, suction pipe, and delivery
    pipe. During operation, the rotating impeller creates centrifugal force, drawing
    liquid into the pump and discharging it at higher pressure. \nCentrifugal pumps
    are widely used in water supply, irrigation, chemical industries, power plants,
    and HVAC systems. From an engineering perspective, understanding pump characteristics,
    efficiency, head, discharge, cavitation, priming, and the affinity laws is essential
    for proper pump selection, design, operation, and maintenance, ensuring reliable
    and energy-efficient performance.\r"
